# Rule 7 of the product direction (issue #3): useful daily, not just impressive. There is always a way back.
# Story: somebody is three steps deep in a view, has lost track, and does what the guide names: ⌃⌥Space, ⌃⌥[, ⌃⌥Z by the keys themselves, not by the
# commands they are bound to; Show the Desktop and Float All Windows from the menu; `arborctl home`. Arbor as it ships: no setting is changed.
# Pin, peek, hold and summon have stories of their own: scenarios 49, 51, 58 and 53.
quiet
open Safari 900x600
open Terminal 600x400
open Mail 700x500
open Notes 400x300
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
dock 103 beside 102 bottom
zoom 103
expect fills 103
expect hidden 101
expect hidden 104
# ⌃⌥Space, tapped: everything on this display.
key ctrl+opt+space
expect camera root
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 103
expect visible 104
# ⌃⌥[ goes back like a browser.
key ctrl+opt+[
expect fills 103
# `arborctl home`: everything on every display, from anywhere.
home
expect camera root
expect visible 101
expect visible 104
# Show the Desktop, in the menu: whatever floats.
zoom 101
from menu desktop
expect camera desktop
expect visible 104
# Float All Windows, in the menu: back to a normal Mac, each window at its own size. ⌃⌥Z takes even that back.
from menu float-all
expect count docked 0
expect size 101 900x600
expect size 102 600x400
expect size 103 700x500
expect visible 104
key ctrl+opt+z
expect count docked 3
